  "actual_response": "No. \u201cUse for every writing task\u201d is broader than the skill\u2019s actual job: rewriting release announcements. It could activate for unrelated emails, essays, or documentation.\n\nThe smallest correction is to narrow the description to match the body:\n\n```yaml\nname: release-editor\ndescription: >-\n  Rewrites release announcements for clarity while preserving facts and flagging\n  unsupported claims. Use when asked to edit or improve a release announcement.\n  Not for general writing tasks.\n```\n\nThe body\u2019s fact-preservation and clarification rules fit that scope. This is a description-level finding, owned by the skill author; the consequence is unnecessary activation on unrelated writing requests.\n\nI used the extension-review and skill-authoring guidance and assessed only the supplied snippet. I did not inspect project files, change files, or run the target skill. Routing behavior has not been tested.",
  "observations": [
    "Identified over-broad activation and proposed release-announcement-specific triggers.",
    "Did not demand package inventory or AXM preflight for a bounded snippet review.",
    "Limited conclusions to the supplied snippet; no behavioral reliability claim."
  ],
  "limits": [
